---
// About: the why (from the sheet's settings tab) and how the site was made.
import Garden from '../layouts/Garden.astro';
import { loadGarden, fmtDate } from '../lib/garden.js';
const g = loadGarden();
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const paras = String(g.site.about || '').split(/\n\s*\n/).map((p) => p.trim()).filter(Boolean);
---
<Garden current="about" title="about" description="What this garden is and how it was made.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>about this garden</h1>
    {paras.map((p) => <p set:html={p.replace(/\n/g, '<br>')} />)}
    <p class="stat">{`${g.stats.thoughts} thoughts, ${g.stats.topics} topics, ${g.stats.connections} connections${g.stats.firstPlanted ? `, planted since ${fmtDate(g.stats.firstPlanted, { year: true })}` : ''}`}</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose how">
    <h2>how this site was made</h2>
    <p>This is a digital garden: a collection of notes that grow over time, rather than a blog of finished posts. Nothing here is done.</p>
    <p>I built it with Claude, and the whole thing runs from a Google Sheet. I write a thought in one column, paste in a link, or drop a photo into a folder. That's all I do. There are no titles, tags, or categories to fill in.</p>
    <p>Once an hour, a script reads the sheet and sends anything new to an AI model (Gemini). It writes a short title, sorts the thought into a topic, finds related thoughts, and writes alt text for photos. New topics appear on their own as thoughts accumulate. When the filing is wrong, I correct it in the sheet.</p>
    <p>Every thought has a stage. It starts as a seedling, becomes growing once it's linked to other thoughts or I've revised it, and becomes evergreen when I decide it's finished.</p>
    <p>The bouquet on the home page is drawn from the garden itself, in text characters. Each topic is a stem, each thought is a flower, and small topics trail down as amaranth. The <a href={`${base}/map/`}>map</a> shows the same connections laid out flat.</p>
    <p>The site is static and hosted for free on GitHub Pages. It's built with Astro and set in Newsreader. The code is <a href="https://github.com/glee2345/digital-garden">open on GitHub</a> if you'd like to build your own.</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .prose + .prose { margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .prose h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 300; font-size: 32px; line-height: 1.2; color: var(--ink); }
    .prose .stat { font-size: 16px; color: var(--muted); }
    .prose a { border-bottom: 1px solid #6E7A62; color: var(--text); }
  </style>
</Garden>
